hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20551","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from 'Alqamah ibn 'Abdullah al-Muzani, from men among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him fear Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, and honor his neighbor; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him fear Allah and honor his guest; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him fear Allah and speak truth or remain silent."
"20552","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from 'Alqamah ibn 'Abdullah al-Muzani, from men among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he mentioned the like of it."
"20553","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Nasr ibn 'Asim, from a man among them, that he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and accepted Islam on condition that he would pray only two prayers, so he accepted that from him."
"20554","Hushaym informed us, 'Ali ibn Zayd informed us, al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: And a man from Banu Salit informed me, he said: I was brought to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I heard him say: The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim; he does not wrong him nor forsake him. Piety is here, piety is here, twice or thrice, and he pointed with his hand to his chest."
